---
// A term's page, which Konzilo's integration puts at the address of each
// taxonomy whose site-description.json declares one, such as
// `"address": "/category/{slug}/"` (astro.config.mjs names it in
// `termPage`). The demo model declares none, so no term has a page until a
// taxonomy does. Konzilo's termPages() gives each term
// of the taxonomy its pages: the term, its posts of every type that takes
// the taxonomy, newest first, ten a page, those of the terms below it among
// them, from a second page on the pager, at /category/<slug>/page/2/ and
// on, and the text for a term with no post, in the site's language, the
// site's own or the core's. The page shows the term's name and its
// description, then its posts as the presentation `list` shows them, with
// their dates and excerpts, and the layout gives Konzilo's Head the term,
// so that its head says the term's name and description, links its feed,
// makes a later page noindex and gives the page its breadcrumbs. The page
// is no post's body, so it is not in the body class. Konzilo gives it
// `term`, the term's entry; `page`, from 1; `posts`, `pager` and `empty`, as
// a presentation's; `taxonomy`, { name, label }, the taxonomy's name, its
// key in a query, and its label; `settled`, { taxonomy, term }, the
// taxonomy's name and the term's slug; and `list`, what the term's whole
// list holds, as a presentation's, its `type` null where several types take
// the taxonomy, which a presentation that filters is handed, to leave out
// the row `settled.taxonomy`, send the settled term with a search and say
// how many posts the term holds. This page uses none of these three.
import { termPages } from '@kntnt/konzilo/astro/post-lists';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import List from './List.astro';

export async function getStaticPaths({ routePattern }) {
  return termPages(routePattern);
}

const { term, page, posts, pager, empty } = Astro.props;
---
<Site entry={term} page={page}>
  <main class="term-page">
    <h1>{term.data.name}</h1>
    {term.data.description && <p class="term-description">{term.data.description}</p>}
    <List posts={posts} options={{ date: true, excerpt: true }} empty={empty} pager={pager} />
  </main>
</Site>
